   "text": {
    "L1": "A symmetrical figure has two matching halves on opposite sides of a mirror line.",
    "L2": "A common mistake is to copy a half and slide it across. That is not a mirror image.",
    "L3": "To reflect a point, count its squares to the mirror line.",
    "L4": "Then count the same number of squares on the other side, straight across.",
    "L5": "With a standing line, the point stays in the same row and moves left or right.",
    "L6": "The shape is flipped, so its size and shape match but its direction changes.",
    "L7": "With a lying line, points move up or down. A point on the line stays where it is.",
    "L8": "Now check the dot: it is 2 squares left of a standing line. Tap its mirror position."
   },
